00:34:13,084 --> 00:34:16,179
What is? Tell me.

485
00:34:17,422 --> 00:34:18,742
The police have
reason to believe

486
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:21,257
that Tom didn't work
late Tuesday night.

487
00:34:21,426 --> 00:34:23,588
He was with Melissa Ann Jones.

488
00:34:27,165 --> 00:34:30,226
- I'd like you to leave.
- Oh, Mrs. McGuire, I'm sorry.

489
00:34:30,402 --> 00:34:32,564
Get out. How dare
you come into my house

490
00:34:32,737 --> 00:34:35,104
and tell me something like that?

491
00:34:35,273 --> 00:34:40,075
- I want you to leave.
- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

492
00:34:44,616 --> 00:34:45,948
- No.
- It's not like

493
00:34:46,117 --> 00:34:48,797
they're gonna be in your living
room. Won't even know they're there.

494
00:34:48,954 --> 00:34:50,889
Probably be just me
and Detective Garrison.

495
00:34:51,056 --> 00:34:53,150
- I can take care of myself.
- I'm telling you,

496
00:34:53,325 --> 00:34:54,691
- this man is dangerous.
- Ben.

497
00:34:54,859 --> 00:34:56,293
- We believe more...
- Ben.

498
00:34:56,461 --> 00:34:57,929
Than we ever did he's the one...

499
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,793
Oh, my gosh. Oh,
I'm so sorry. Tom. Hi!

500
00:35:00,966 --> 00:35:05,165
- Hi. I come at a bad time?
- Oh, just being my usual klutzy self.

501
00:35:05,337 --> 00:35:06,930
Maybe you'd like to
go to the men's room

502
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:09,631
and clean that up, sir.
You can use my rag.

503
00:35:11,509 --> 00:35:13,603
- Hi.
- Hi.

504
00:35:30,228 --> 00:35:32,857
- Not bad for a starving actress.
- Heh.

505
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:38,463
Well, my grandmother sends
me a big fat check every month.

506
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:44,167
And starving isn't exactly the word
I would use to describe my thighs.

507
00:35:44,609 --> 00:35:46,601
Oh, I don't know about that.

508
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:52,815
- You're embarrassing me.
- Why?

509
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:56,580
You're a beautiful woman.
You shouldn't put yourself down.

510
00:35:57,489 --> 00:35:59,822
Really? You joined
this date club thing?

511
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:05,453
Oh, no, no, I didn't join. I didn't
give them any money or anything.

512
00:36:05,630 --> 00:36:11,228
It's just that, I don't
know, he talked me into it.

513
00:36:11,636 --> 00:36:13,434
How did it work out?

514
00:36:13,972 --> 00:36:15,463
Well, I had two dates.

515
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:18,109
The first one was fair,

516
00:36:18,276 --> 00:36:22,008
and the second one, I'm
lucky to be here talking to you.

517
00:36:22,647 --> 00:36:25,742
- What did she...?
- She came on.

518
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:31,754
I mean, she pretty well had me
down for the count in the restaurant.

519
00:36:32,390 --> 00:36:35,986
I hid out in the men's
room till she left.

520
00:36:36,161 --> 00:36:38,281
You better go out with some
nice lady from the church.

521
00:36:38,430 --> 00:36:40,899
You got that part right.

522
00:36:42,133 --> 00:36:45,831
- Oh, Tom, wait.
- It's okay.

523
00:36:46,771 --> 00:36:49,468
Mm. No, wait a minute.

524
00:36:51,276 --> 00:36:52,835
If I wanted a roll in the hay,

525
00:36:53,011 --> 00:36:56,607
I would go out with one
of those bozos I wait on.

526
00:36:56,781 --> 00:36:58,750
Not you.

527
00:36:58,917 --> 00:37:00,317
Life is short, Jerri.

528
00:37:00,485 --> 00:37:01,612
I know.

529
00:37:01,786 --> 00:37:05,484
So why don't you give me a
little time to get to know you?

530
00:37:09,828 --> 00:37:11,319
What are you doing?

531
00:37:11,496 --> 00:37:14,557
Leaving. I've got a
meeting in the morning.

532
00:37:16,501 --> 00:37:18,993
Am I gonna hear from you again?

533
00:37:19,504 --> 00:37:20,699
We'll see.

534
00:37:40,692 --> 00:37:42,092
There he goes.

535
00:37:56,241 --> 00:37:59,302
If he stays true to
form, he'll be back.

536
00:38:06,451 --> 00:38:09,182
- So he never came back?
- No.

537
00:38:09,354 --> 00:38:12,290
Detective Garrison
was just a little upset.

538
00:38:12,457 --> 00:38:16,258
Sat there the whole night and
Tom McGuire never showed.

539
00:38:16,427 --> 00:38:18,328
Maybe he smelled a
rat. What did Jerri say?

540
00:38:18,496 --> 00:38:23,958
Jerri said that he got mad
when she put the brakes on,

541
00:38:24,135 --> 00:38:27,367
got up, said he
might call, and left.

542
00:38:27,539 --> 00:38:29,201
Turn it on.

543
00:38:29,374 --> 00:38:31,775
- No way. I'm not gonna get a shock.
- I fixed it.

544
00:38:33,178 --> 00:38:35,113
Then you turn it on.

545
00:38:36,281 --> 00:38:38,682
Hello? Oh, hey, Jerr.

546
00:38:38,850 --> 00:38:43,311
Yeah. Oh, yeah? All
right, I'll definitely tell him.

547
00:38:43,488 --> 00:38:46,788
Right. Okay. Bye-bye.

548
00:38:47,559 --> 00:38:50,188
Tom McGuire called. They're
going out tomorrow night.

549
00:38:50,361 --> 00:38:51,556
Oh.

550
00:38:52,230 --> 00:38:53,892
Well... Hmm?

551
00:38:56,367 --> 00:38:57,892
No, I don't understand.

552
00:38:58,069 --> 00:38:59,749
Why can't you meet
with him in the morning?

553
00:38:59,904 --> 00:39:01,964
Because he leaves for
Europe in the morning.

554
00:39:02,140 --> 00:39:05,042
I'm sorry, hon. I'll make
it up to you. I promise.

555
00:39:05,910 --> 00:39:09,312
Where will you be?
I mean, just in case.

556
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:12,006
I don't know what kind of
dinner arrangements he made.

557
00:39:12,183 --> 00:39:14,550
If you need me,
call the service.

558
00:39:14,719 --> 00:39:16,278
That's what you always say.

559
00:39:18,223 --> 00:39:19,782
What's wrong?

560
00:39:23,161 --> 00:39:25,995
Nothing. Good luck.

561
00:39:43,581 --> 00:39:45,141
Well, this time
something better happen.

562
00:39:45,283 --> 00:39:47,252
That's all I gotta say.

563
00:39:49,187 --> 00:39:52,282
You know, I'm gonna go to Savannah
to visit some friends this weekend.

564
00:39:52,457 --> 00:39:53,618
Wanna come?

565
00:39:53,791 --> 00:39:55,817
Oh, I don't think
I can get away.

566
00:39:56,427 --> 00:39:57,895
Work?

567
00:40:00,064 --> 00:40:01,088
- Tom!
- What?

568
00:40:01,266 --> 00:40:03,360
Stop it. We've been
through this before.

569
00:40:03,534 --> 00:40:06,800
You said you needed to
know me. You know me.

570
00:40:07,739 --> 00:40:09,264
- No!
- Wait a minute.

571
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:11,409
You agreed to go out
with me again, didn't you?

572
00:40:11,576 --> 00:40:14,740
I agreed to go out with you,
not to jump in bed with you.

573
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:16,673
What's the big deal?
Grow up, for God's sake.

574
00:40:16,814 --> 00:40:17,873
Grow up?

575
00:40:18,216 --> 00:40:21,846
I'll tell you what. When I
grow up, I'll give you a call.

576
00:40:22,020 --> 00:40:23,545
Hey.

577
00:40:24,889 --> 00:40:26,881
Life is very short, Jerri.

578
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:31,025
You're gonna be
sorry you didn't do this.

579
00:40:31,195 --> 00:40:33,721
Just shut up and go.

580
00:40:41,039 --> 00:40:43,201
Y'all come back now, you hear?

581
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:51,581
- Looks mad.
- Yeah, good.

582
00:41:29,787 --> 00:41:31,779
Somebody's in there with her.

583
00:41:36,961 --> 00:41:39,123
- Hold it right there.
- You all right?

584
00:41:39,297 --> 00:41:40,526
Yeah.

585
00:41:40,698 --> 00:41:42,929
He came out of nowhere.

586
00:41:47,605 --> 00:41:51,007
Well, I'll be. Daniel Price.

587
00:41:51,909 --> 00:41:54,469
The guy who owns
the dating service?

588
00:41:54,645 --> 00:41:56,944
Looks like he tried to
do the same thing to you

589
00:41:57,115 --> 00:41:59,346
he did to Melissa Ann Jones.

590
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:01,042
Why would he wanna kill me?

591
00:42:01,753 --> 00:42:03,085
Yeah.

592
00:42:03,254 --> 00:42:06,088
Fred Golub messed
it up for you, didn't he?

593
00:42:06,257 --> 00:42:09,523
Because you wanted to frame
Tom McGuire for Melissa's murder,

594
00:42:09,694 --> 00:42:11,526
but Fred screwed
it up, didn't he?

595
00:42:11,696 --> 00:42:13,631
I don't know what
you're talking about.

596
00:42:14,532 --> 00:42:17,502
Why would he wanna frame
Tom? I thought they were friends.

597
00:42:17,668 --> 00:42:19,569
Yeah.

598
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:23,002
No.

599
00:42:24,776 --> 00:42:29,874
Bob, you know, I wonder, could
you trace a call for me, like, right now?

600
00:42:30,615 --> 00:42:32,345
Sure.

601
00:42:41,125 --> 00:42:43,117
Mrs. McGuire?

602
00:42:43,961 --> 00:42:46,157
Hi, I'm Ben Matlock.

603
00:42:46,330 --> 00:42:49,994
Do you mind if Detective
Garrison here has a listen?

604
00:42:50,168 --> 00:42:52,797
He won't hear anything, will he?

605
00:42:52,970 --> 00:42:55,997
We know that call's going
to Daniel Price's house.

606
00:42:56,174 --> 00:42:58,405
And we all know
Daniel isn't home.

607
00:42:58,576 --> 00:43:00,067
We called the phone company.

608
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:03,014
- Nothing.
- Aha.

609
00:43:03,181 --> 00:43:04,205
As soon as you called,

610
00:43:04,382 --> 00:43:06,408
Daniel put the phone
down on his end

611
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:08,075
and rushed over to
that woman's house

612
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:10,687
your husband was
out with tonight.

613
00:43:10,855 --> 00:43:13,051
Make it seem like he's on
the phone with somebody

614
00:43:13,224 --> 00:43:14,988
when actually he's
out committing murder.

615
00:43:15,159 --> 00:43:18,789
That's very clever, to use the
telephone to establish an alibi.

616
00:43:18,963 --> 00:43:20,226
That your idea or his?

617
00:43:20,398 --> 00:43:22,198
I really don't know
what you're talking about.

618
00:43:22,333 --> 00:43:24,529
That's just what Daniel said.

619
00:43:24,702 --> 00:43:26,762
But he'll change his
tune when he finds out

620
00:43:26,938 --> 00:43:28,372
you've been arrested too.

621
00:43:28,906 --> 00:43:32,638
I imagine he'll lie his head off,
say the whole thing was your idea.

622
00:43:32,810 --> 00:43:35,302
Especially when he
realizes his chance of getting

623
00:43:35,480 --> 00:43:38,211
any of your husband's
money has gone down to zip.

624
00:43:38,382 --> 00:43:40,908
That is not true. Daniel...

625
00:43:43,321 --> 00:43:45,620
You were gonna
say Daniel loves you?

626
00:43:48,359 --> 00:43:50,794
I'm sure he does.

627
00:43:55,500 --> 00:43:57,025
- How did it go?
- Fine.

628
00:43:57,201 --> 00:43:59,401
When the two of them saw
each other in the booking area,

629
00:43:59,537 --> 00:44:01,697
it was a race to see which
one could cut a deal faster.

630
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:05,600
- Who won?
- Brenda. Yeah, she was the first.

631
00:44:05,776 --> 00:44:07,438
She said it was
all Daniel's idea.

632
00:44:07,612 --> 00:44:10,411
Heh. So much for true love, huh?

633
00:44:10,581 --> 00:44:14,211
As it turns out, Tom did try to break
in to that woman's apartment last year.

634
00:44:14,385 --> 00:44:16,047
And he told Daniel about it.

635
00:44:16,220 --> 00:44:18,917
And Daniel and Brenda
figured they'd copy him.

636
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:20,690
And that way the woman
might come forward

637
00:44:20,858 --> 00:44:23,089
- when Tom was charged with murder.
- Well, why?

638
00:44:23,261 --> 00:44:24,593
- Why did they do it?
- Money.

639
00:44:24,762 --> 00:44:28,164
They figured if he was in
jail, they could take the dough.

640
00:44:28,633 --> 00:44:30,693
So, Fred, you are off the hook.

641
00:44:30,868 --> 00:44:32,860
- Well, I can't thank you guys enough.
- Oh.

642
00:44:33,037 --> 00:44:37,873
And for going beyond the call of
duty, I'm gonna take you out to lunch.

643
00:44:38,042 --> 00:44:40,307
How about Saturday?

644
00:44:41,345 --> 00:44:42,711
Uh...

645
00:44:44,215 --> 00:44:46,616
Well, I, uh... I'm gonna
be in a tennis tournament.

646
00:44:46,784 --> 00:44:47,979
Well, how about Sunday?

647
00:44:48,152 --> 00:44:50,553
I'm gonna be river rafting.

648
00:44:50,721 --> 00:44:52,451
How about now? We
go get some dessert.

649
00:44:52,623 --> 00:44:54,353
I know this great
frozen-yogurt place.

650
00:44:54,525 --> 00:44:56,824
Fred, please.

651
00:44:57,295 --> 00:44:59,662
You know, you don't
have to go anywhere.

652
00:45:00,131 --> 00:45:01,997
We can have dessert right here.

653
00:45:02,166 --> 00:45:04,158
You go in the
living room, relax,

654
00:45:04,335 --> 00:45:06,236
Jerri and I'll scrounge
around and find cookies.

655
00:45:06,404 --> 00:45:08,202
Cliff will make some
coffee. How about it?

656
00:45:08,973 --> 00:45:10,271
- Great.
- Okay.

657
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:14,975
You go ahead.
I'll cover for you.

658
00:45:15,479 --> 00:45:19,177
Bless you, Ben. I'm gonna
get even with you for this, Cliff.

659
00:45:19,350 --> 00:45:21,319
What did I do?

660
00:45:21,886 --> 00:45:23,821
Okay, if I turn on
some lights in here?

661
00:45:23,988 --> 00:45:25,616
Do whatever you want.

662
00:45:25,790 --> 00:45:28,624
That lamp by the
couch. Turn that on.

663
00:45:30,895 --> 00:45:32,227
Oh.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
